  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "In which of the following relations is $y$ a function of $x$?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "$y^2=x$",
    "B": "$|y|=x$",
    "C": "$y=3x-2$",
    "D": "$x^2+y^2=1$"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Only in \\(y=3x-2\\) does each value of \\(x\\) correspond to a unique value of \\(y\\). For A and B, \\(x=1\\) gives both \\(y=1\\) and \\(y=-1\\). For D, \\(x=0\\) gives both \\(y=1\\) and \\(y=-1\\). Each of these three relations therefore fails the uniqueness requirement. The answer is C.",
